<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Brazil presidential election heads to runoff as Bolsonaro leads Lula</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:775a6a65b07d11f017e96aad816f691f26dd007dd78ff6ff548e81a9506fad2f</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:56:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T00:16:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula--792d040be18d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261005-brazil-presidential-election-runoff-bolsonaro-lula" /><summary type="html">Right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro pulled off a surprise first-place finish ahead of President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva in Sunday's election, which heads to a run-off vote on October 25 as neither clinched a majority.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>A Profile of Brazil's Potential President</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8202c11e6bb05b8dccf5ae09d5c9a953a64de27b1ab37627df9ba654895c3aca</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T18:34:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261004-a-profile-of-brazil-s-potential-president--ddef5eefc576.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261004-a-profile-of-brazil-s-potential-president" /><summary type="html">France 24's Gavin Lee speaks to Brazil analyst Henrique Tavares Furtado about how Flavio Bolsonaro is pledging to reshape the country, and asks: who is the man behind the political persona?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil heads to the polls for high-stakes election between Lula and Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c634fca50fff9787af80620399a453a01a51917362047591a12b8276a07c848e</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:38:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-heads-to-the-polls-for-high-stakes-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro--00531a37ca37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-heads-to-the-polls-for-high-stakes-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Woman at centre of Cornell gang rape lawsuit targeted with threats, lawyer says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32f2d17a07e896373906adb16de88d2d02739ebf62dbbf34d260162d6f26628</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T16:25:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-woman-at-center-of-cornell-gang-rape-allegations-targeted-with-threats-jane-doe--374a939685ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-woman-at-center-of-cornell-gang-rape-allegations-targeted-with-threats-jane-doe" /><summary type="html">The woman who alleged that she was drugged and raped by seven male students at a Cornell University fraternity house has been the target of threats, her lawyer told CNN on Sunday. Cornell's president earlier voiced support for an external review of the Ivy League institution facing widespread outcry over its handling of the case.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Lula and Bolsonaro tied in polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94df5ec81ea117fa72a66d525ec141ffbb13baa764224fb353e845894f716b04</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:19:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls--985ac9bf96f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-lula-and-bolsonaro-tied-in-polls" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Mara Nogueira, Senior Lecturer in Urban Geography at Birbeck, University of London, says the tight race reflects the consolidation of two political camps, with many Brazilians voting not out of support for a candidate, but to keep the other out of power. She points to the cost of living, religion and social media echo chambers as key factors shaping the vote, alongside a major banking scandal that has so far had limited impact on Flavio Bolsonaro’s campaign.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula de Silva: 80-year-old incumbent Brazilian president seeks 4th term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:771cd56ad0744fbd75a7462699969e763bacdede99d573aaad9b78a834b581b7</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term--6f4499fd648a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-de-silva-80-year-old-incumbent-brazilian-president-seeks-4th-term" /><summary type="html">Brazilians began casting their votes on Sunday in a closely watch presidential election pitting incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former president Jair Bolsonaro. Nearly 160 million voters will also pick lawmakers, senators and governors in an election that will determine whether Latin America's biggest nation follows a regional swing to the right championed by US President Donald Trump. France 24 correspondent Jan Onoszko tells us the latest from Rio de Janeiro.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro face off in Brazil presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8a642256372353e6bcb714236dc59d59693a1895d270982039eb04f70013250</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:56:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race--d6b55874ce57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/lula-and-bolsonaro-face-off-in-brazil-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the presidential race is centred on two rivals: President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator. Dr Andrea Aruska de Souza Santos, Director of King's College Brazil Institute in London, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cornell president breaks silence over alleged campus rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91c945a7371c7fb831138d0b9611d48aeb092a030cce39a93be2ac18845ec5b9</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:53:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape--cdaa86cfffd3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cornell-president-breaks-silence-over-alleged-campus-rape" /><summary type="html">Cornell University remains at the centre of controversy over an alleged gang rape at a fraternity on campus, with the university president now breaking his silence. In an eight-minute video statement released Saturday night, Michael Kotlikoff called the allegations, made by a woman known as Jane Doe, deeply disturbing and said the university must do better. Shirli Sitbon has this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>Polls close in Brazil's high-stakes election pitting Lula against Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b8f9a92fabf213ec7c13408795e1ab34fac908b7e453169ba4c5d8987dc92dc</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T11:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro--de08e320fb32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-brazilians-start-voting-in-tight-election-between-lula-and-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians voted Sunday in a high-stakes presidential election pitting incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva against far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, following a campaign dominated by corruption scandals, economic anxiety and accusations of US meddling. The knife-edge election comes at a moment when the region is shifting to the right in line with the Trump administration.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: A portrait of Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb9949229853513a7cb93f31c7ac1b2ec760cc928f5811a212e32204638ef20b</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T09:49:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-a-portrait-of-flavio-bolsonaro--a98c600b2f2f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-a-portrait-of-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">Brazilians are voting for governors and lawmakers, but the biggest stakes are in the presidential race. Twelve candidates are on the ballot, but the contest is seen as a toss-up between President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and Flavio Bolsonaro. Lula is seeking a fourth and final term, warning that Brazil’s sovereignty is at stake amid pressure from Donald Trump. Bolsonaro, meanwhile, has highlighted his ties to the White House, saying Brazil needs better deals with the US, including over its rare mineral resources. Nick Rushworth has more on the controversial senator.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil polls open in a few hours</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a973802e499fdd865262f44eb500b9007d0f5e987b493de0ec77a0600de51d5</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:25:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-polls-open-in-a-few-hours--33059de87308.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-polls-open-in-a-few-hours" /><summary type="html">Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his main challenger Flavio Bolsonaro wrapped up their campaigns on Saturday in the powerhouse state of Sao Paulo, where a fifth of the nation's vote is based, seeking to rally supporters and convince the undecided on the eve of Sunday's nail-biter election. Mareeke Reethof, lecturer in Latin American Politics at the University of Liverpool, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flock's AI tracking sparks privacy fears and violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdddbb9acbcd95c77abd6a98951be7260e308cf57960ad7b3bbe62a18dfdea74</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:23:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/flock-s-ai-tracking-sparks-privacy-fears-and-violence--402730ac99e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/flock-s-ai-tracking-sparks-privacy-fears-and-violence" /><summary type="html">In the US, Flock Security cameras form an AI-powered surveillance network that records licence plates and other vehicle information. Their controversial use has become a political issue ahead of the midterm elections, and the cameras are increasingly being targeted by vandals. Caitlin Brown explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ossoff and El-Sayed: Two Senate races and what they say about the Democratic Party</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dfe30089d35a29031fe42300e00f726fcc47f1d06aa10d4b8a3852675ac82e7</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T07:21:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-ossoff-and-el-sayed-two-senate-races-and-what-they-say-about-the-democratic-party--af765eac41b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261004-ossoff-and-el-sayed-two-senate-races-and-what-they-say-about-the-democratic-party" /><summary type="html">Senator Jon Ossoff, a Democratic favourite, is running for re-election in Georgia in the 2026 US midterms while Abdul El-Sayed is a Senate candidate in the battleground state of Michigan. The two Democrats have very different profiles and platforms, underscoring divergences within the party. They could also determine the party's future ahead of the 2028 presidential election.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro make final push for votes ahead of Brazil's knife-edge election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6e7b7f7fbf66fde090362fdf5eefc981d66c3434a9d9ec23387da7286fdb56a</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T20:16:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-lula-and-bolsonaro-make-final-push-for-votes-ahead-of-brazil-s-knife-edge-election--dea208eef413.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-lula-and-bolsonaro-make-final-push-for-votes-ahead-of-brazil-s-knife-edge-election" /><summary type="html">Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his main challenger Flavio Bolsonaro wrapped up their campaigns on Saturday in the powerhouse state of Sao Paulo, where a fifth of the nation's vote is based, seeking to rally supporters and convince the undecided on the eve of Sunday's nail-biter election.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro in final push for votes ahead of Brazil's knife-edge election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76e6677aee674b0f661244d3f28b2bbf49b18759ba56cfb1d6cc92d363c79c58</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T20:10:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261003-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-final-push-for-votes-ahead-of-brazil-s-knife-edge-election--ae9e0c623640.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261003-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-final-push-for-votes-ahead-of-brazil-s-knife-edge-election" /><summary type="html">Brazil's President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his main challenger Flavio Bolsonaro made their final pitch to voters Saturday with rallies in the pivotal state of Sao Paulo ahead of a nail-biter election that has been marred by scandals and mudslinging.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tennessee prison chief who oversaw botched Christa Pike execution resigns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7399ec0333396b1195d0454ab9e027ea278215f184415eb8e8f3065a7132a935</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T17:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-tennessee-prison-chief-who-oversaw-botched-christa-pike-execution-resigns--070a60d4707d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-tennessee-prison-chief-who-oversaw-botched-christa-pike-execution-resigns" /><summary type="html">The head of Tennessee's prison system has resigned in the first major shake-up since the stunning failed execution of convicted murderer Christa Pike, who is in critical condition after surviving two lethal injections. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee, who previously denied Pike clemency, has halted further executions through the rest of the year while a review is conducted.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro: In the name of the father, sons, and holy ideology</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed4c4ee8ee8de412daa922898eb749d27b3a7fd7bc6e0ebb2c9105d163c22e0a</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T09:48:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology--9892326d1899.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology" /><summary type="html">The first round of Brazil’s presidential election on Sunday pits two well-known names in the political ring: Lula vs. Bolsonaro. But it’s not former president Jair Bolsonaro facing off against the incumbent head of state – it’s his eldest son, Flavio Bolsonaro. He’s less charismatic than his father but just as ideologically radical as the family patriarch.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil’s Lula gears up for ‘last dance’ with run for fourth presidential term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10a4fd6202eca46e2178caf745d16910dfd674f47694fafea8262c029352af95</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:20:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term--5b44a3117a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term" /><summary type="html">President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will stand for re-election in Brazil on Sunday. At 80, the former steelworker hopes to capitalise on his popularity and economic successes to win a fourth term in office but is neck-and-neck in the polls with far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Who is presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28ab24aa7c6c1114124ae262351e9f96c2b34148e087243bbec2d670f312080e</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T15:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-who-is-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro--529bdce9ea36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-who-is-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">He was still relatively unknown in Brazil just a few months ago. The 45-year-old senator is now neck and neck with incumbent President Lula in the polls for the upcoming presidential election. Flavio Bolsonaro's victory would add Brazil to the long list of Latin American countries that have shifted to the right or far right in recent months.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Cornell 7: Allegations spark fury over gang rape culture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1af30c35c7560684287faf5b759e75bdf655dcdba2848ccfdcb20bb30133bf16</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture--c1482a18eb2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture" /><summary type="html">How allegations of a gang rape at an American Ivy League university have set social media alight, sparking widespread fury over the way colleges and universities handle sexual assault cases. Also the French parliament is currently debating a major new bill aimed at tackling violence against women and children. But does it go far enough? Annette Young asks Dr Andreea Gruev-Vintila, a social psychologist who assisted with the drafting of the legislation. Plus the king of Morocco names Marrakesh mayor, Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri, as the country's first female prime minister.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>What the media got right and wrong about Cornell gang rape case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b8b4f41414739ba3f84157930301f669befcd8eeaff44638ab7cdfe1f68e429</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:53:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case--863be3ca8b9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case" /><summary type="html">The alleged gang rape at America's Cornell University has shocked many people around the world and raised questions about institutional failure and toxic masculinity. The story was first broken by student journalists and national media soon followed, thrusting it in the spotlight. While there has been excellent reporting, the story has also exposed failures in how some pieces framed officials' statements alongside Jane Doe's allegations. We take a closer look in Scoop.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>Paraguay, a tax and political haven for Brazil's far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7bf636f1fadbab337d672c52873f409c899e2c76d07ad68dd458949c78533c3</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T12:48:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right--68deff3b0c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right" /><summary type="html">Over the past five years, applications for residence permits submitted by Brazilians in Paraguay have more than doubled. Many of them are Bolsonaro supporters who are afraid October's presidential election will be won by incumbent leader Lula – whom they accuse of plunging the Latin American giant into an unprecedented economic crisis. FRANCE 24's Fanny Lothaire, Valeria Saccone and Mélanie Blondeau report, with Jan Onoszko.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>What's real and what's fake? How AI is impacting Brazil's election race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e66c157979a81db65ee4b72a242efacc96675dc5dd143ea231c171e73a5c858b</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:34:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race--0b74a4095735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race" /><summary type="html">With just two days to go before the first round of Brazil's presidential election, artificial intelligence is taking centre stage, whether it's a deepfake avatar of former president Jair Bolsonaro to support his son's candidacy, or an AI-generated working-class female voter criticising President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. According to the Brazilian intelligence agency, disinformation will be one of the main challenges of this election. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's election: Lula or Bolsonaro Jr?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abf57f4c962c03a5be2e7616fa5ee31814cc48ad5df4ff4afc1a72b61178bca5</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:04:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr--90417820582f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 2: We look at reactions in the French papers after high school blockades turned violent across France. We also look ahead to Brazil's two-round presidential election, which begins this weekend. The electoral campaign culminated with the cancellation of a presidential debate after both President Lula and his rival Flavio Bolsonaro pulled out. Finally, this year's Comedy Wildlife Awards finalists do not disappoint.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro’s mudslinging heats up ahead of weekend vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8aed14c4df42302b090b8469130d8d2606b7c45c0b4154515b157f0175c2854</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T05:44:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-s-mudslinging-heats-up-ahead-of-weekend-vote--9b234ebd94f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-s-mudslinging-heats-up-ahead-of-weekend-vote" /><summary type="html">The mudslinging between Brazil’s incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his election rival, Flavio Bolsonaro, has heated up ahead of what is expected to be an extremely close vote this weekend. From stating loose rumours as facts, to taking comments completely out of their context, they are both doing everything they can to win a few more votes.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US continues to be 'a very significant partner', UN peacekeeping chief says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfeee40e37e6a3c2deccc3bdd4d8c23af5be4b4e45f8ba720ac77db2e735e24c</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:14:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief--b044ef9ba027.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN peacekeeping chief Jean-Pierre Lacroix said the US continues to be "a very significant partner", despite owing $3 billion to peacekeeping. With the UN forced to cut about 25 percent of its capacity, Lacroix defended missions that cost just 0.2 percent of global military spending: "Peacekeeping is a good deal really."</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Convicted killer Christa Pike in ‘critical condition’ after two lethal injections fail to kill her</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf53f75b692d6d6bfd01220f0bcffc029a507b796b7ad1412217aa3d842ce3fc</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T05:32:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections--aeb8f625e4e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike, who has been on death row in Tennessee for more than 30 years for torturing and murdering a classmate, was on Wednesday set to be executed, but the lethal injections meant to kill her failed. Pike was then transported to a medical facility, where her attorney says she remains in a "critical condition".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>El Salvador sets date for 2027 presidential election as Bukele seeks third term</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c4b0664df9d4d2e144a31175cb352b4bdfaaeb682c1bbc080aa591f0eebc650</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T02:32:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term--90fb5878abea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term" /><summary type="html">El Salvador will hold presidential elections on February 28, 2027, the electoral tribunal said Wednesday, opening the way for President Nayib Bukele to seek a third term after constitutional changes removed presidential term limits. Bukele has drawn praise for sharply reducing gang violence but faced criticism over rights abuses during his crackdown.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump renews calls for former Federal Reserve chief Jerome Powell's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d224aa210918602c7c1e57d4d3fc50f611c058912877efce9167d504323dfff8</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:44:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation--58eead028846.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation" /><summary type="html">The Federal Reserve's watchdog on Wednesday found no grounds for a criminal referral over a roughly $1 billion cost overrun on renovations to the central bank's Washington buildings, while faulting project oversight. The findings prompted President Donald Trump to renew his call for former Fed chief Jerome Powell to resign.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery clears legal hurdle</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7696211dca11b7c4462134f0d0c86350888e050f691fe550ccc08a8ba7e4d1c5</id><updated>2026-10-05T05:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T22:19:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle--68378233ae13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle" /><summary type="html">A federal judge on Wednesday approved a settlement clearing Paramount’s takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery after 12 US states challenged the deal on antitrust grounds. The agreement includes safeguards for CNN’s editorial independence and requires the merged studio to release at least 30 films a year for its first two years.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry></feed>
